Example Evolution Scenario
Day 1: Deploy "Full Stack Web Team v1"
- Designer → Developer → Copywriter

Day 5: After 10 uses, system notices:
- Designer always needs researcher for competitor analysis
- Evolution: Adds researcher, creates v1.1

Day 10: After 25 uses:
- Developer bottleneck on complex React components
- Evolution: Adds "React Specialist", creates v1.2

Day 20: Major task needs accessibility
- Evolution: Forks to "Accessible Web Team v1.0"
- Adds accessibility specialist
- Modifies workflow to include a11y checks

Result:
- Original team still exists (proven reliable)
- Evolved versions for specific needs
- Forked variants for specialized tasks

My Recommendation

Create 10-15 high-quality base templates manually
Create 3-5 proven group templates
Build observation/metrics from day 1
Enable controlled evolution after baseline proven
Keep all versions (can always rollback)

This gives you:

Immediate value (templates work now)
Future flexibility (can evolve)
Safety rails (no crazy mutations)
Learning system (gets better over time)